Ponytail
--------
The lean-change discipline (skills/lean-change, skills/senior-review,
commands/lean|review|audit|debt.md, lib/lean.js) adapts ideas from Ponytail by
DietrichGebert - https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail - studied at commit
09c434ab73ca43761c5d8b0c5d341926c2fba710 (2026-10-18). Adapted ideas include:
the reuse-first decision ladder and the list of things never cut, one small
test for non-trivial logic, "shortcut:" comments naming a limit and an upgrade
trigger plus a ledger of them (the marker convention is kept compatible on
purpose), a map of existing top-level definitions so reuse costs no search,
review and audit ordered correct > safe > load > tested > fast > lean with a
concrete case required for every finding, and not reporting "savings" without
a real baseline. ECCode's text and code are its own; it adds engine checks at
task completion and per-task measurements. See docs/lean.md.

