Benchmark material from other projects (bench/suites/realbugs)
--------------------------------------------------------------
The realbugs benchmark tasks are real bugs catalogued by BugsInPy
(https://github.com/soarsmu/BugsInPy, commit 11c5f1eea954a42132cfd06bf257766a7963e0fd):
its metadata picked the buggy and fixed commits and the tests that show each
bug. For each task the suite keeps, unmodified, the test files of the fixed
commit (<task>/hidden/files/) and the fix itself as a patch
(<task>/reference/fix.patch). They are used only to check benchmark runs and
remain under their projects' licenses:

  youtube-dl  https://github.com/ytdl-org/youtube-dl  public domain (The Unlicense)
  black       https://github.com/psf/black            MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018 Łukasz Langa
  tornado     https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado   Apache License 2.0
  thefuck     https://github.com/nvbn/thefuck         MIT License, Copyright (c) 2015-2022 Vladimir Iakovlev
  tqdm        https://github.com/tqdm/tqdm            MIT License and, for files so marked in its
                                                      LICENCE, Mozilla Public License 2.0
                                                      (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/)

The projects' source code itself is not in this repository: the benchmark
fetches each buggy commit from the project's own repository when it runs.

Benchmark subject (bench/suites/mealie, bench/pilot/mealie)
-----------------------------------------------------------
The Mealie pilot measures ECCode on Mealie
(https://github.com/mealie-recipes/mealie), which is distributed under the
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0. No Mealie file is in this
repository: the tasks name upstream commits, and the benchmark exports the
source and the upstream fixes' own tests from a local mirror of Mealie's
repository when it runs. The requests in bench/suites/mealie/_tools/prompts.json
were written for the pilot; the duplicate check in bench/suites/mealie/_hidden/
holds only hashes, no Mealie code. Reports name files, functions and counts
and quote ECCode's own output, never Mealie source.
